scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: the-expanse
run_id: 2
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase distinguished NotFound from other errors in from_file_or_default.
    The config tests cover loading and env overrides but not error discrimination.
    Reviewer flagged silent ignore of invalid env values but not the broader from_file_or_default
    swallowing issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM] CWE-209: ServerError passes through arbitrary
    strings with no sanitization at error.rs:8-9, noting the test is vacuous and attacker-controlled
    response body would be printed verbatim.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: --tenant accepts raw String instead of
    validated TenantId at cli.rs:29, noting axiathon-core has a TenantId type that
    should be used. TEA also wrote header injection prevention tests for CRLF in tenant,
    but did not require TenantId type usage.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified workspace dependencies as correct. The code changes
    summary shows Cargo.toml was modified with +2 lines (uuid and chrono added). No
    phase flagged that direct version strings were used instead of workspace = true
    for those additions.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: Config silently accepts unknown fields\
    \ \u2014 no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] at config.rs:8, noting a typo like sever_url\
    \ would silently use default."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. The reviewer noted a different vacuous test (server_error_display)
    but missed this specific one.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via let _ = config. TEA wrote config tests but did not identify this gap in assertion
    coverage.
